      "action_taken": "Passed the turn without casting any spells, leaving 8 mana unused.",
      "better_line": "Cast Wan Shi Tong, Librarian for X=4 (5/5 flier, draw 2 cards) leaving up Spell Pierce or Spell Snare to protect it, or X=6 for maximum value as a 7/7 drawing 3 cards. The opponent has no creatures to contest it and limited known removal options.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 179,
      "player": "Gem3F Valley",
      "decision_index": 277,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Wan Shi Tong, Librarian during own main phase when it has flash. With no creatures on board threatening lethal and countermagic (Spell Pierce, Spell Snare) in hand, the optimal line is to pass the turn and cast Wan Shi Tong at the opponent's end step, preserving the ability to counter opponent's spells during their turn.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Wan Shi Tong, Librarian during precombat main phase",
      "better_line": "Pass the turn holding up Spell Pierce/Spell Snare, then cast Wan Shi Tong at opponent's end step for the same value while maintaining countermagic flexibility during opponent's turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 178,
      "player": "Gem3F Valley",
      "decision_index": 274,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Valley has Demolition Field available and the opponent has Ba Sing Se (a nonbasic land) on the battlefield. Activating Demolition Field during combat or at end of opponent's turn would destroy a key nonbasic land that enables earthbend activations, while also thinning their own deck for a basic. Additionally, if the opponent searches their library, it would trigger Wan Shi Tong's ability when cast later. More importantly, Gem3F Valley could flash in Wan Shi Tong, Librarian at end of combat/step with available mana (they have 8 lands). With X=3 they'd get a 4/4 flyer and draw 1 card, establishing a clock and card advantage. Passing without doing anything wastes the opportunity to use mana productively at instant speed.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority during combat without activating any abilities or casting any spells.",
      "better_line": "Flash in Wan Shi Tong, Librarian for X=3 (spending 5 mana total) to establish a 4/4 flying vigilance threat and draw a card, or at minimum activate Demolition Field to destroy Ba Sing Se and deny earthbend activations.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 181,
      "player": "Gem3F Valley",
      "decision_index": 280,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Valley passed with 8 lands available and two copies of Wan Shi Tong, Librarian in hand at end of turn. Flashing in Wan Shi Tong at end of opponent's turn is a standard play to use mana efficiently - it avoids sorcery-speed removal, and the opponent has no creatures on board to pressure with. With X=3 (paying 3UU), they'd get a 4/4 flyer with vigilance and draw 1 card, or X=4 (4UU) for a 5/5 and draw 2. This is a mana sink that should be used at end of opponent's turn rather than letting mana go to waste. The opponent has only lands and enchantments on board with no creatures, so there's minimal risk. Passing here wastes the opportunity to deploy a threat efficiently.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting anything, leaving all mana unused.",
      "better_line": "Flash in Wan Shi Tong, Librarian for X=3 or X=4 at end of opponent's turn to deploy a flying threat and draw cards while holding up the second copy and countermagic for future turns.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 182,
      "player": "Gem3F Valley",
      "decision_index": 280,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Discarding Icetill Explorer over a basic Forest when they have Fabled Passages that can already fetch Forests. Icetill Explorer is a powerful engine card that enables extra land drops (synergizing with the 5 lands in hand), plays lands from graveyard, and triggers landfall for Earthbender Ascension. Having a backup copy is valuable against removal, especially since the opponent has shown access to removal spells.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Icetill Explorer",
      "better_line": "Discard a basic Forest instead, since Fabled Passage can fetch Forests and the second Icetill Explorer provides redundancy for their key engine piece against an opponent with removal",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 183,
      "player": "GPT4om Analyst",
      "decision_index": 283,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Gem3F Valley passed with no action when they could cast Wan Shi Tong for X=6 (7/7 flying vigilance, draw 3 cards) against an empty board. The opponent has no creatures and limited removal options in mono-green for a large flyer. This was the perfect window to deploy a game-winning threat.",
      "action_taken": "Passed the turn without casting any spells, despite having 8 mana and Wan Shi Tong in hand against an empty board.",
      "better_line": "Cast Wan Shi Tong, Librarian for X=6, creating a 7/7 flying vigilance creature and drawing 3 cards. This establishes a dominant board presence and card advantage against an opponent with no creatures and no easy answers to a large flyer.",
      "type": "blunder",
